  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Emergency Integrated Primary Health Care to Drought-Affected Communities in Sool, Sanaag, and Bari Regions of Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CERF project will contribute to nutrition recovery through provision of emergency primary health care to communities in northern Somalia, where the severely food insecure population is at the highest risk of sliding from Crisis on the Integrated Food Security Phase Classification scale (IPC3) to Emergency (IPC4). Through deployment of mobile medical response teams, the project will contribute to objectives one and two of the 2019 Humanitarian Response Plan, namely, to reduce acute humanitarian needs and excess mortality, and to reduce emergency levels of acute malnutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
